,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":7270.424124231,"data":" Create a short, concise summary of the paper based on its abstract.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":7270.424129863,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":7270.424134124,"data":"Few-shot learning (FSL) is one of the key future steps in machine learning and raises a lot of attention. In this paper, we focus on the FSL problem of dialogue understanding, which contains two closely related tasks: intent detect \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":7270.424139433,"data":"---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":7270.42414759,"data":" The paper presents a new FSL benchmark called FewJoint, designed to address the challenge of joint learning in few-shot scenarios. The paper introduces FewJoint, a corpus containing 59 different dialogue domains from real industrial APIs, making it easier for researchers to conduct FSL experiments. The paper also finds that insufficient performance in few-shot settings can lead to noisy sharing between two sub-tasks, causing disturbance in joint learning. To overcome this issue, the paper proposes a novel trust gating mechanism that ensures high-quality sharing by blocking low-confidence intents. Additionally, the paper introduces a Reptile-based meta-learning strategy to improve generalization in unseen few-shot domains. The proposed method achieves significant improvements on two datasets and outperforms existing methods. \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":7270.424180129,"data":"[finished: True ]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":7270.424183626,"data":"================================================================================ \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":7270.424187078,"data":" Is there a meaning for Christmas wreaths? \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":7270.424190629,"data":"---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":7270.424194316,"data":" Yes, there is a significant meaning behind the Christmas wreath. The wreath represents the idea of eternal life and hope in Christ's death on the cross. It symbolizes the enduring presence of God's love and compassion in our lives, as well as the hope that we can find comfort and peace through His sacrifice.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":7270.424198559,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":7270.424202328,"data":"The wreath also holds symbolic significance, with each color representing different aspects of Christ's nature: red symbolizing bloodshed, white symbolizing purity, green symbolizing new beginnings, gold symbolizing wealth and prosperity, and silver symbolizing eternity.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":7270.424206556,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":7270.424211635,"data":"Overall, the Christmas wreath serves as a reminder of the importance of faith, hope, and love in our lives, and reminds us to hold onto those values even during difficult times. \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":7270.424215853,"data":"[finished: True ]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":7270.424219502,"data":"================================================================================ \n"}
